@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core. Remove future provider coordination from core DFD and add private media/manual follow-up flows.
title MVP DFD Level 1 — core content and application information
skinparam backgroundColor #0D1525
skinparam defaultFontColor #EDF4FF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam wrapWidth 190
actor "Private owner" as U
actor "Employer viewer" as V
rectangle "Resumefolio core" {
 rectangle "F01 establish invited identity\nEnforce scoped authority" as I
 rectangle "F02 maintain independent profile / resumes\nPreview/select/apply; separately publish" as P
 rectangle "F03 PDF / selected protected sharing\nDirect / byte-range admission" as S
 rectangle "F04 manual applications\nActual materials / status / next action / follow-up" as A
 rectangle "F09 private My Files & Media\nType / size / quota / recovery" as F
 database "Core-owned records" as D
 folder "Private bytes on same core server" as B
 I --> D : account / current grants
 P --> D : source / draft / publication identities
 A --> D : actual submission manifests / progress
 F --> B : admitted private bytes
 S --> B : only currently authorized selected bytes
 P --> S : explicit publication selection
}
U --> P : intended edits
U --> A : manual application data
U --> F : upload / external link
V --> S : exact protected representation request
note bottom of A
 F05 private mail/calendar is AFTER MVP in an independent API system.
 Manual follow-up requires no provider account.
end note
@enduml
